  "outstanding_asks": [
    {
      "by": "cubic-dev-ai",
      "ask": "<!-- cubic:v=707bc86f-98b2-40a4-b46c-4cd5add50f22 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=b06f62a6-f05e-58cb-ad38-d4644c45127a -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":8} -->\nP2: A fork cannot safely install a different resolver: `set_name_resolver()` mutates the shared state classes and their global name caches, so rebuilding names for one app changes the other app's wire names. Make resolver-dependent state/var caches context-aware, or reject differing resolvers for contexts sharing these classes.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid \u2014 if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At packages/reflex-base/src/reflex_base/registry.py, line 272:\n\n<comment>A fork cannot safely install a different resolver: `set_name_resolver()` mutates the shared state classes and their global name caches, so rebuilding names for one app changes the other app's wire names. Make resolver-dependent state/var caches context-aware, or reject differing resolvers for contexts sharing these classes.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -152,8 +266,10 @@ def fork(self) -> Self:\n+            _states_by_default_name=dict(self._states_by_default_name),\n             decorated_pages=list(self.decorated_pages),\n             bundled_libraries=list(self.bundled_libraries),\n+            name_resolver=self.name_resolver,\n             _explicit_bundled_libraries=dict(self._explicit_bundled_libraries),\n         )\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>",
      "addressed": false,
      "path": "packages/reflex-base/src/reflex_base/registry.py",
      "outdated": false
    },
    {
      "by": "greptile-apps",
      "ask": "<a href=\"#\"><img alt=\"P1\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p1.svg?v=9\" align=\"top\"></a> **Old events survive compilation**\n\nEvents built under an earlier minified scheme can pass `raise_for_stale_names` unchanged. A module-level `LiteralEventVar` can store `a.b.c`; after the handler's ID changes to `d`, the default-name scan cannot match `a.b.c`, and the state-local scan does not inspect event strings. Compilation succeeds with an event the backend no longer registers\u2014or now assigns to another handler.\n\nThe bundle carries the current scheme digest, so the handshake does not catch this. Track resolved event names when they are built, or rebuild these event Vars when installing the resolver.",
      "addressed": false,
      "path": "reflex/minify.py",
      "outdated": false
    },
    {
      "by": "cubic-dev-ai",
      "ask": "<!-- cubic:v=b6c5521f-cc6b-42ef-8aca-252ecb3c27dd -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=7177db7f-231d-5ad2-b62d-fa3dff7bde98 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":9} -->\nP2: This drops empty resolver segments, so registry keys diverge from the event names emitted by `format_event_handler` for a valid custom resolver. Preserve the formatter\u2019s `handler.state is None` branch to keep inbound event dispatch consistent.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid \u2014 if so, understand the root cause and fix it. When an issue isn't valid or won't be fixed in this PR, reply in its thread with the reason and then resolve the thread. At packages/reflex-base/src/reflex_base/registry.py, line 76:\n\n<comment>This drops empty resolver segments, so registry keys diverge from the event names emitted by `format_event_handler` for a valid custom resolver. Preserve the formatter\u2019s `handler.state is None` branch to keep inbound event dispatch consistent.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -59,6 +59,23 @@ def _rekey(\n+    \"\"\"\n+    from reflex_base.utils.format import get_event_handler_parts\n+\n+    return \".\".join(filter(None, get_event_handler_parts(handler)))\n+\n+\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n```suggestion\n    state, name = get_event_handler_parts(handler)\n    return name if handler.state is None else f\"{state}.{name}\"\n```",
      "addressed": false,
      "path": "packages/reflex-base/src/reflex_base/registry.py",
      "outdated": false
    },
    {
      "by": "cubic-dev-ai",
      "ask": "<!-- cubic:v=d443d037-ab92-4992-b957-0d24c3655302 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=7177db7f-231d-5ad2-b62d-fa3dff7bde98 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":7} -->\nP2: This live-name check can accept an event for a handler removed by a state reload because it consults the old issuer's resolver mapping without checking the current event registry. Verify that each issuer still has the recorded handler registered before returning it as live; otherwise compilation can emit an event the backend no longer handles.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid \u2014 if so, understand the root cause and fix it. When an issue isn't valid or won't be fixed in this PR, reply in its thread with the reason and then resolve the thread. At reflex/minify.py, line 766:\n\n<comment>This live-name check can accept an event for a handler removed by a state reload because it consults the old issuer's resolver mapping without checking the current event registry. Verify that each issuer still has the recorded handler registered before returning it as live; otherwise compilation can emit an event the backend no longer handles.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -735,17 +735,53 @@ def _renamed_default_references() -> dict[str, str]:\n+    for state_cls, handlers in issuers.items():\n+        state_name = state_cls.get_full_name()\n+        for handler in handlers:\n+            if f\"{state_name}.{ctx.get_handler_name(state_cls, handler)}\" == name:\n+                return None\n+            labels.append(f\"event handler {get_state_full_path(state_cls)}.{handler}\")\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>",
